When the context is canceled or expired, continuing to iterate over the remaining templates in the outer loop is inefficient and will result in unnecessary, immediately-failing RPC calls. Instead of breaking the inner retry loop, we should return early from `deleteTaskTemplates` with the accumulated errors and the context error. This also allows us to simplify the code by removing the `retryLoop` label.

```go
		for attempt := 0; attempt < 5; attempt++ {
			delErr = r.client.DeleteActorTemplate(ctx, atespace, name)
			if delErr == nil || status.Code(delErr) == codes.NotFound {
				delErr = nil
				break
			}
			if ctx.Err() != nil {
				return errors.Join(append(errs, ctx.Err())...)
			}
			select {
			case <-ctx.Done():
				return errors.Join(append(errs, ctx.Err())...)
			case <-time.After(500 * time.Millisecond):
			}
		}
```

